 Nepal's ousted PM Oli over shootout that killed 19 protesters</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/124020458.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/south-asia/gen-z-group-demands-arrest-of-nepals-ousted-pm-oli-over-shootout-that-killed-19-protesters/articleshow/124020458.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/south-asia/gen-z-group-demands-arrest-of-nepals-ousted-pm-oli-over-shootout-that-killed-19-protesters/articleshow/124020458.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-21T00:32:06+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124020501,imgsize-1409659.cms"/></item><item><title>Saudi Customs seizes over 261,000 Amphetamine pills and nearly 10 kg of Meth in four smuggling busts</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/124020237.cms" /&gt;Saudi Customs thwarted four major smuggling attempts, seizing over 261,000 amphetamine pills and nearly 10 kilograms of methamphetamine at Jeddah Airport, Duba Port, and Al-Batha border crossing. Coordinated efforts with the General Directorate of Narcotics Control led to three arrests. Authorities urge the public to report suspicious activities via a confidential hotline, offering rewards for valuable information.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/saudi-customs-seizes-over-261000-amphetamine-pills-and-nearly-10-kg-of-meth-in-four-smuggling-busts/articleshow/124020237.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/saudi-customs-seizes-over-261000-amphetamine-pills-and-nearly-10-kg-of-meth-in-four-smuggling-busts/articleshow/124020237.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-21T00:38:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124020532,imgsize-855975.cms"/></item><item><title>Saudi Arabia issues new packaging rules for fruits and vegetables: What suppliers and vendors must know</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/124008705.cms" /&gt;Saudi Arabia has introduced new regulations requiring clear labeling and durable, food-safe packaging for fruits and vegetables sold in local markets. Issued by the Ministry of Environment, Water and Agriculture (MEWA), the rules aim to enhance food safety and sustainability. MEWA, established in 1953, oversees agricultural standards, including packaging, to support public health and Vision 2030 goals.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/saudi-arabia-issues-new-packaging-rules-for-fruits-and-vegetables-what-suppliers-and-vendors-must-know/articleshow/124008705.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/saudi-arabia-issues-new-packaging-rules-for-fruits-and-vegetables-what-suppliers-and-vendors-must-know/articleshow/124008705.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-21T00:09:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124020150,imgsize-1761739.cms"/></item><item><title>‘Monsters’: Trump demands Venezuela repatriate prisoners from US</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/124019192.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/monsters-trump-demands-venezuela-repatriate-prisoners-from-us-warns-of-incalculable-consequences/articleshow/124019192.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/monsters-trump-demands-venezuela-repatriate-prisoners-from-us-warns-of-incalculable-consequences/articleshow/124019192.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-20T23:54:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124019849,imgsize-932482.cms"/></item><item><title>‘President had no idea’: Karoline Leavitt denies White House role in ABC shelving Kimmel</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/124018134.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/president-trump-had-no-idea-karoline-leavitt-denies-white-house-role-in-abc-shelving-jimmy-kimmel-blasts-obama/articleshow/124018134.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/president-trump-had-no-idea-karoline-leavitt-denies-white-house-role-in-abc-shelving-jimmy-kimmel-blasts-obama/articleshow/124018134.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-20T22:51:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124018591,imgsize-103734.cms"/></item><item><title>'Heat of moment': Expelled Texas State student who mocked Charlie Kirk's assassination</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/124017447.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/heat-of-moment-texas-state-student-who-mocked-charlie-kirks-assassination-expelled-teen-regrets-mistake/articleshow/124017447.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/heat-of-moment-texas-state-student-who-mocked-charlie-kirks-assassination-expelled-teen-regrets-mistake/articleshow/124017447.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-20T21:35:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124017923,imgsize-1005197.cms"/></item><item><title>‘Sophie, not Nicholas’: Justice Brett Kavanaugh attacker 'adopts' female identity</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/124016850.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/refer-as-sophie-brett-kavanaugh-attacker-adopts-female-identity-nicholas-remains-legal-name/articleshow/124016850.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/refer-as-sophie-brett-kavanaugh-attacker-adopts-female-identity-nicholas-remains-legal-name/articleshow/124016850.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-20T20:20:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124017053,imgsize-142256.cms"/></item><item><title>Saudi's Bitcoin Trading Laws 2025 : What traders and businesses need to know</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/124017628.cms" /&gt;Saudi Arabia adopts a cautious yet evolving approach to Bitcoin and cryptocurrencies. While retail trading faces warnings and banking restrictions, the kingdom explores blockchain technology, CBDC pilots, and regulatory sandboxes. This indicates a carefully managed path toward formal frameworks, prioritizing institutional engagement and compliance with AML/KYC regulations for future market participation.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/saudis-bitcoin-trading-laws-2025-what-traders-and-businesses-need-to-know/articleshow/124017628.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/saudis-bitcoin-trading-laws-2025-what-traders-and-businesses-need-to-know/articleshow/124017628.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-20T21:44:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124017939,imgsize-160338.cms"/></item><item><title>Trump’s $100,000 ‘Pay-to-Play’ H-1B visa rule sparks outcry, immigration attorneys gear up to file suits</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/124014488.cms" /&gt;Donald Trump's new rule impacts H-1B visa holders. A $100,000 fee is needed for entry after September 21, 2025. This affects many Indians awaiting US jobs. Legal challenges are expected. The policy raises concerns about fairness. Experts predict uncertainty for businesses and professionals. The proclamation's legality is under scrutiny. It may face court injunctions soon.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trumps-100000-pay-to-play-h-1b-visa-rule-sparks-outcry-immigration-attorneys-gear-up-to-file-suits/articleshow/124014488.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trumps-100000-pay-to-play-h-1b-visa-rule-sparks-outcry-immigration-attorneys-gear-up-to-file-suits/articleshow/124014488.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-20T16:26:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Lubna Kably</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124014472,imgsize-46378.cms"/></item><item><title>Trump’s new Gold Card: Fast-Track residency for the wealthy generates debate</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/124015109.cms" /&gt;</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trumps-new-gold-card-fast-track-residency-for-the-wealthy-generates-debate/articleshow/124015109.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trumps-new-gold-card-fast-track-residency-for-the-wealthy-generates-debate/articleshow/124015109.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-20T17:18:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Lubna Kably</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124015206,imgsize-3951261.cms"/></item><item><title>Trump H-1B Visa Hike: Why UAE, Saudi, Qatar might be better options for Indians looking to go abroad</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/124013708.cms" /&gt;Trump’s $100,000 H-1B visa fee has slammed the door on average Indian tech talent, making the U.S. dream increasingly elusive. Meanwhile, the Gulf is rolling out the red carpet, offering tax-free income, long-term visas, and booming tech ecosystems. For skilled Indians, the future may no longer lie in Silicon Valley, but in Dubai, Riyadh, and Doha.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/trump-h-1b-visa-hike-why-uae-saudi-qatar-might-be-better-options-for-indians-looking-to-go-abroad/articleshow/124013708.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/trump-h-1b-visa-hike-why-uae-saudi-qatar-might-be-better-options-for-indians-looking-to-go-abroad/articleshow/124013708.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-20T19:01:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124016289,imgsize-1682735.cms"/></item><item><title>In Numbers: H-1B was already tough for Indians; Donald Trump's 100,000 fee just made it tougher</title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/124014678.cms" /&gt;The H-1B programme was created in 1990 with a cap of 65,000 visas per year, later expanded to include 20,000 extra slots for US master’s degree holders. That total of 85,000 visas has not changed in over a decade, even as America’s economy and demand for skilled workers exploded.</description><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-numbers-h-1b-was-already-tough-for-indians-donald-trumps-100000-fee-just-made-it-tougher/articleshow/124014678.cms</link><guid>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-numbers-h-1b-was-already-tough-for-indians-donald-trumps-100000-fee-just-made-it-tougher/articleshow/124014678.cms</guid><pubDate>2025-09-20T18:40:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-124016091,imgsize-98938.cms"/></item></channel></rss>